# No Cursor attribution

Do not add `Co-authored-by: Cursor`, `Made-with: Cursor`, or any other Cursor attribution trailer to commits, pull requests, or code comments. The human adds attribution only when they choose to.

- Never pass `--trailer` (or equivalent) for Cursor authorship on `git commit`.
- After every commit, check `git log -1 --format=%B`. If a Cursor trailer was injected by the tooling, amend immediately to remove it when the amend rules in `ship-issue` allow it; otherwise tell the human before rewriting history.
- Prefer the project's `.githooks/commit-msg` hook (when `core.hooksPath` points at `.githooks`) as the last line of defense.
